// Copyright (c) 2026 Roshan. All rights reserved.// Proprietary license — see LICENSE file for details.package com.roshan.persona.selfmodify.diimport com.roshan.persona.brain.skill.sandbox.JsSandboximport com.roshan.persona.selfmodify.RhinoJsSandboximport com.roshan.persona.selfmodify.SelfModifyEngineimport dagger.Moduleimport dagger.Providesimport dagger.hilt.InstallInimport dagger.hilt.components.SingletonComponentimport javax.inject.Singleton/** * NOUS — Self-modify Hilt module (Module 15 — Self-modify). * * Wires the real Rhino JS sandbox into Brain's DI graph. Strategy §14.2 * Table 3 + Table 10 — this module replaces Brain's `FakeJsSandbox` and * `NoOpJsSandbox` with the real [RhinoJsSandbox] implementation. * * ## Flavor gating (ADR 0008) * * This entire module lives in `src/selfmodify/kotlin/` — a custom source * dir added to BOTH the `dev` and `internal` flavors (see * `feature/selfmodify/build.gradle.kts`). In the `prod` flavor: * *  - This file is NOT compiled → [SelfModifyModule] is absent from the *    Hilt graph. *  - `RhinoJsSandbox` is NOT compiled → no references to *    `org.mozilla.javascript.*` exist in the prod APK. *  - The `org.mozilla:rhino:1.7.15` dependency is declared as *    `devImplementation` + `internalImplementation` only → Rhino JAR is *    NOT bundled in the prod APK. *  - Brain's `NoOpJsSandbox` (always-fails stub) is used instead. * * This satisfies ADR 0008's "Play Store safe" requirement: no JS engine * code in the prod APK, no surface for Play reviewers to flag. * * ## Interface overrides (Strategy §14.2 Table 10) * * | Brain interface | Real impl (this module) | Replaces | * |-----------------|--------------------------|----------| * | [JsSandbox] | [RhinoJsSandbox] | Brain's `FakeJsSandbox` (test stub) + `NoOpJsSandbox` (prod stub) | * * Brain does NOT provide its own `JsSandbox` binding — when this module * is absent (prod flavor), any class that injects `JsSandbox` will fail * to compile in prod. Currently NO class injects `JsSandbox` (the brain * module's `BrainModule` doesn't bind it), so prod compiles fine. * * When a future Brain component needs `JsSandbox`, the `:app` module's * prod source set should bind `NoOpJsSandbox` explicitly (e.g., via a * `prod`-flavor Hilt module in `:app`). * * @see RhinoJsSandbox * @see SelfModifyEngine * @see <a href="docs/adr/0008-self-modifying-js-flavor-gated.md">ADR 0008</a> */@Module@InstallIn(SingletonComponent::class)object SelfModifyModule {    /**     * Provide [RhinoJsSandbox] as Brain's [JsSandbox] interface.     *     * `@Singleton` because:     *  - The Rhino [org.mozilla.javascript.ContextFactory] is expensive to     *    construct (initializes global state).     *  - We want all sandbox executions to share the same factory (so the     *    instruction-count observer is consistent across calls).     *     * Note: [RhinoJsSandbox] itself is also annotated `@Singleton @Inject`     * — Hilt will use its constructor directly. This `@Provides` is     * redundant but kept for explicitness (matches the pattern in     * `:feature:security`'s `SecurityModule`).     *     * @param impl the concrete Rhino sandbox (injected by Hilt via     *   [RhinoJsSandbox]'s `@Inject constructor`).     * @return the sandbox, exposed as Brain's [JsSandbox] interface.     */    @Provides    @Singleton    fun provideJsSandbox(impl: RhinoJsSandbox): JsSandbox = impl    /**     * Provide [RhinoJsSandbox] as a concrete type (for [SelfModifyEngine]     * to inject directly if it ever needs Rhino-specific APIs not on the     * [JsSandbox] interface).     *     * Redundant with the `@Inject constructor` on [RhinoJsSandbox] — kept     * for explicitness and to match the pattern in other NOUS feature     * modules.     */    @Provides    @Singleton    fun provideRhinoJsSandbox(): RhinoJsSandbox = RhinoJsSandbox()    /**     * Provide [SelfModifyEngine] as a singleton.     *     * `@Singleton` because:     *  - The engine holds an in-memory skill registry (`ConcurrentHashMap`)     *    that must persist across skill invocations for the app's lifetime.     *  - Re-creating the engine on each injection would lose all stored     *    skills (defeating the entire point of self-modification).     *     * Note: [SelfModifyEngine] itself is also annotated `@Singleton @Inject`     * — Hilt will use its constructor directly. This `@Provides` is     * redundant but kept for explicitness.     */    @Provides    @Singleton    fun provideSelfModifyEngine(engine: SelfModifyEngine): SelfModifyEngine = engine}